USB MIDI host: felucca-bsp pull request #7 by Kerem Kilic (keremimo), "feat(usb): port Melodee USB MIDI host under
MPL-2.0", https://github.com/hugelton/felucca-bsp/pull/7, head ea3d2e3ce2a67d2ee3d986a44b4dab4d86fcfea5, open when
taken (2026-10-25). The diff below is that pull request's, unchanged (https://github.com/hugelton/felucca-bsp/pull/7.diff).
When felucca-bsp merges it, bump the submodules and delete this patch.
What it adds: FELUCCA_USB_HOST=1, the USB-C port as the host of a USB-MIDI device (controller in, synth out),
directly or behind one powered hub; docs/USB_HOST.md is its contract. MIDIMON's tap of the host's input is
patches/felucca-bsp/0002-midi-tap-usb.patch; fm1-base's API for apps is patches/fm1-base/0002-usb-host.patch.
Why MIDIMON needs it: a USB-MIDI controller or synth plugged into the FM-1 itself, monitored and reached by THRU.

Origin and licence (the pull request's own NOTICE and LICENSING.md record the source commits): Melodee's USB host,
GPL-3.0-only in Melodee, ported to felucca-bsp under MPL-2.0 on its authors' word:
  Adrien Tibi (Recursive Field Instruments), in Melodee pull request #75: keremimo asked
  (https://github.com/keremimo/melodee/pull/75#issuecomment-6383989315), verbatim:
    "Are you okay with licencing your part of the code as MPL? That would enable me to get this code into the
     fm1_base and also Saadet as well."
  and Adrien answered (https://github.com/keremimo/melodee/pull/75#issuecomment-6384184014), verbatim:
    "Hey! Excellent. It works super well here. I've been using various controllers and that's so convenient.
     For the licensing, of course, feel free to do so :)
     Kind regards,
     Adrien Tibi (Recursive Field Instruments)"
  Kerem Kilic, for his part (MIDI out, recovery, tests, felucca-bsp integration), in felucca-bsp pull request #7's
  description (https://github.com/hugelton/felucca-bsp/pull/7), verbatim:
    "I also license my contributions to this port under MPL-2.0."
These are the only grounds for this code being MPL-2.0; a build with Bluetooth links JieLi's binary libraries, so no
GPL code may be in it (MIDIMON's LICENSING.md).
Applies to: felucca-bsp d6b8f77 (fm1-base aa2b3bc). Upstream: it is upstream's own pull request.

